Add environment variables to existing .env files.

Subcommands: • service (or infra): Add vars for any catalogue id (e.g., postgresql, vercel) • framework: Add vars for a framework (e.g., django) • blueprint: Add vars from a stack blueprint • custom: Interactive custom variable addition

Exit codes: 0 when the variables were added, were already there, the run was a --dry-run, or you backed out of a menu or a custom question (Esc); 2 when it could not run (unknown id, bad argument, no terminal to ask, a write error); 4 you answered no (or Esc) at the write confirmation.

Usage: evnx add [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  service    Add variables for a service, infrastructure target or framework [aliases: infra]
  framework  Add variables for a framework
  blueprint  Add variables from a stack blueprint (without overwriting existing)
  custom     Add your own variables: as arguments, or one prompt at a time
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --list
          List every id `add` takes: services, infrastructure, frameworks and blueprints

      --dry-run
          Show what would be added, skipped and kept; write nothing. Needs no terminal

      --json
          Print the result as one JSON document on stdout (needs --yes or --dry-run: it never asks)

  -p, --path <PATH>
          Output path (default: current directory)
          
          [default: .]

      --env-name <NAME>
          Write to `.env.<NAME>` instead of `.env` (one file per run; loop over names for several). `prod` and `.env.prod` both work. Defaults to `[defaults] env_name`

      --example <FILE>
          The template to add names to, from the project folder. Default: the environment's own (`.env.<NAME>.example`) when there is one, else `[defaults] example`, else `.env.example`

      --no-template
          Write only the env file: no names into the template, and no template created. For a server that keeps `.env.prod` alone

  -y, --yes
          Skip confirmation prompts

  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output

  -q, --quiet
          Print nothing on success. Findings, warnings, errors and requested data still print

      --no-color
          Disable colored output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Full guide: https://docs.evnx.dev/cli/commands/add
